  summary: Surprise! A tomato is really a fruit, a juicy berry full of tiny seeds.
  facts:
  - Wild tomatoes first grew in the Andes Mountains of South America!
  - The word tomato comes from tomatl, a word in the Aztec language.
  - Tomatoes aren't only red. They can be yellow, green or even purple!
  - Tomatoes are cousins of eggplants! Their leaves are poisonous, so only eat the
    fruit.
  sources:
  - Encyclopaedia Britannica. Tomato. https://www.britannica.com/plant/tomato
  - University of Minnesota Extension. Crop and field planning tools for vegetable
    farmers. https://extension.umn.edu/agriculture/specialty-crops/vegetable-farming/crop-and-field-planning-tools-for-vegetable-farmers
  realGrowTime: about 65 to 85 days after planting outside (50 to 70 for cherry tomatoes)
  realHarvestPattern: Farmers stake or cage the plants to keep the fruit off the
    ground!
